\tag{fdip}
\title{Signs of the connection weights}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A determinant over the real numbers can be negative even
when its operator is self-adjoint. The massive cochain kernel
and the massive Wilson kernel have different positivity
hypotheses. Small sign examples and a finite norm bound
make those hypotheses explicit before a connection law is used.}

